    "uncited": [
     "*   **Step Advancement:** Advance the ray by the distance to the nearest surface.",
     "*   **Self-Shadowing:** If the ray starts exactly at the surface point ($t=0$), the SDF query returns $0$, causing immediate false occlusion.",
     "*   **Linear Drop-off Artifacts:** Using a linear denominator for the distance ratio (e.g., $h/t$) can cause severe shadow artifacts when light sources are very close to objects, as the ratio changes rapidly.",
     "*   **Precision:** If $h$ is very small but not below the threshold, the ratio $h/t$ becomes small, correctly darkening the shadow.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$, where $N$ is the number of ray march steps."
    ]
   }
  }
